{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1772836392676,"sessionID":"ses_33ab77fa1ffeaHXObNPEtwU5Wk","part":{"id":"prt_cc5488ddc001IXqK39m72eMWki","sessionID":"ses_33ab77fa1ffeaHXObNPEtwU5Wk","messageID":"msg_cc548812d001Q2irtNclcPEdRL","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_vlopb3dg8rb2_1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/paule/MAD/.tmp/add-code-path-to-board.instructions"},"output":"<path>/home/paule/MAD/.tmp/add-code-path-to-board.instructions</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: You are a senior software architect reviewing a feature plan.\n2: \n3: ## Feature: add code path to board\n4: \n5: ### Original Description:\n6: Add a code path and context file to each board's configuration so that AI agents know where the associated project code lives and have access to project-level context whenever they are invoked. A board lives inside the project it represents (e.g., ~/mycode/.mad/boards/myboard), so the root code path is derivable, but it should be made explicit. Two additions: (1) a `code_path` field in ~/.mad/config.json pointing to the project root, and (2) a ~/.mad/CONTEXT.md file for free-form project context. Agents should also be started with their working directory set to the project root, not the individual work item directory. Every time an agent is invoked, its instructions should include the code path and the path to CONTEXT.md at the top.\n7: \n8: ### Generated Plan:\n9: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1772836375475,\"sessionID\":\"ses_33ab7ce6cffeKY4KUUDy0n9FCY\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_cc5484bb1001JUWI4ra7kAZ16M\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_33ab7ce6cffeKY4KUUDy0n9FCY\",\"messageID\":\"msg_cc548326c001UhNohFWcXGzNyv\",\"type\":\"step-start\",\"snapshot\":\"568732f58a520ec881a3dc3fddd8cb5b1b05fa19\"}}\n10: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1772836376313,\"sessionID\":\"ses_33ab7ce6cffeKY4KUUDy0n9FCY\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_cc5484db1001JrZvU8aEY98fa3\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_33ab7ce6cffeKY4KUUDy0n9FCY\",\"messageID\":\"msg_c